# Ticket #4471 — Calendar and booking date discrepancies

Ticket #4471 merged 427 reports about calendar invites and booking dates not matching. Analysis found six distinct problem types:

## Problems identified

| Problem | Count | Description |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| Wrong day/date shown in calendar invite | 295 | Calendar invites display incorrect dates or days of the week. Examples: invite shows Tuesday when it should be Monday, or completely wrong dates like 4 July instead of 7 April. |
| Other date/invite discrepancy | 52 | Date conflicts between booking and invite that don't fit other patterns. Customers cannot determine which date is correct. |
| Appointment automatically moved | 29 | Appointments appear to shift between dates without user action. Customers report bookings changing dates on their own. |
| Mixed up or conflicting dates | 27 | Multiple conflicting dates in the same booking. Invites contradict what customers agreed to during booking. |
| Date transformation/conversion error | 13 | Date values corrupted or incorrectly converted. Examples: 4 March → 3 April, or 7 April → 4 July (day-month swap pattern). |
| Booking date differs from invite date | 11 | Confirmed booking date does not match the calendar invite. Customer books on one date, receives invite for a different date. |

**Total: 427 reports across 6 distinct problem categories**

## Root cause patterns

The day-month swap pattern in transformation errors (13 reports) suggests localization or date parsing issues, particularly in regions using DD-MM format. The largest category (295 reports of wrong dates) indicates a systemic issue in how dates are formatted or calculated when generating invites.

## Next steps

Each problem type has been filed as a separate issue in the GitHub repo so the engineering team can investigate and fix them independently.

